From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:04:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: emc2305: read a per-channel minimum PWM from the
 device tree

The driver already carries a per-channel pwm_min and applies it in both the
hwmon and cooling paths, but it can only be set through platform data. A
device-tree probe therefore always lands on EMC2305_FAN_MIN, so boards whose
fans stall below a documented minimum duty have no way to express that.

Read an optional microchip,pwm-min from each fan child. The defaults move
into emc2305_probe_childs_from_dt() so a child can override them, and the
device-tree branch of probe no longer resets pwm_min afterwards -- pwm_freq,
the polarity mask and the output mask already survive that branch, and
pwm_min was the sole exception.

A thermal trip cannot substitute for this. It would bound only what the
governor asks for, leaving a direct hwmon write free to take the fan below
the minimum, including to zero.

emc2305_of_parse_pwm_child() releases args.np before returning as of 6.18,
so the rejection path for an out-of-range value releases it too.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 .../bindings/hwmon/microchip,emc2305.yaml     |  9 ++++++++
 drivers/hwmon/emc2305.c                       | 23 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/hwmon/microchip,emc2305.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/hwmon/microchip,emc2305.yaml
index d3f06ebc19fa..2437228e32db 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/hwmon/microchip,emc2305.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/hwmon/microchip,emc2305.yaml
@@ -54,6 +54,15 @@ patternProperties:
           The fan number used to determine the associated PWM channel.
         maxItems: 1
 
+      microchip,pwm-min:
+        description:
+          Minimum PWM duty for this channel, as the raw 0-255 register value.
+          Requests below it, including zero, are raised to this floor. Use it
+          for fans that stall or fail to start below a documented minimum.
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+        maximum: 255
+        default: 0
+
     required:
       - reg
 
diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/emc2305.c b/drivers/hwmon/emc2305.c
index 67e82021da21..a775c3ad0573 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/emc2305.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/emc2305.c
@@ -538,7 +538,7 @@ static int emc2305_identify(struct device *dev)
 static int emc2305_of_parse_pwm_child(struct device *dev,
 				      struct device_node *child,
 				      struct emc2305_data *data)
-{	u32 ch;
+{	u32 ch, pwm_min;
 	int ret;
 	struct of_phandle_args args;
 
@@ -578,6 +578,22 @@ static int emc2305_of_parse_pwm_child(struct device *dev,
 		data->pwm_output_mask |= EMC2305_OPEN_DRAIN << ch;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Optional per-channel minimum duty. A fan that stalls below a
+	 * documented minimum needs that floor to hold on every request, so it
+	 * is kept in pwm_min and applied by the hwmon and cooling paths alike
+	 * rather than being expressed as a thermal trip.
+	 */
+	if (!of_property_read_u32(child, "microchip,pwm-min", &pwm_min)) {
+		if (pwm_min > EMC2305_FAN_MAX) {
+			dev_err(dev, "Invalid microchip,pwm-min %u of %pOFn\n",
+				pwm_min, child);
+			of_node_put(args.np);
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
+		data->pwm_min[ch] = pwm_min;
+	}
+
 	of_node_put(args.np);
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -587,9 +603,12 @@ static int emc2305_probe_childs_from_dt(struct device *dev)
 	struct emc2305_data *data = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct device_node *child;
 	int ret, count = 0;
+	int i;
 
 	data->pwm_output_mask = 0x0;
 	data->pwm_polarity_mask = 0x0;
+	for (i = 0; i < EMC2305_PWM_MAX; i++)
+		data->pwm_min[i] = EMC2305_FAN_MIN;
 
 	for_each_child_of_node(dev->of_node, child) {
 		if (of_property_present(child, "reg")) {
@@ -669,8 +688,6 @@ static int emc2305_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	} else {
 		data->max_state = EMC2305_FAN_MAX_STATE;
 		data->pwm_separate = false;
-		for (i = 0; i < EMC2305_PWM_MAX; i++)
-			data->pwm_min[i] = EMC2305_FAN_MIN;
 	}
 
 	data->hwmon_dev = devm_hwmon_device_register_with_info(dev, "emc2305", data,
-- 
